WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.020
Luke 9

00:02.020 --> 00:09.240
And he called the twelve together and gave them power and authority over all demons and to cure diseases.

00:09.600 --> 00:13.780
And he sent them out to proclaim the kingdom of God and to heal.

00:14.300 --> 00:15.540
And he said to them,

00:15.940 --> 00:20.260
Take nothing for your journey, no staff, nor bag, nor bread, nor money.

00:20.800 --> 00:22.320
And do not have two tunics.

00:22.860 --> 00:26.260
And whatever house you enter, stay there and from there depart.

00:26.260 --> 00:30.420
And wherever they do not receive you, when you leave that town,

00:30.900 --> 00:34.260
shake off the dust from your feet as a testimony against them.

00:34.560 --> 00:39.560
And they departed and went through the villages, preaching the gospel and healing everywhere.

00:40.500 --> 00:45.260
Now Herod the Tetrarch heard about all that was happening, and he was perplexed,

00:45.860 --> 00:49.440
because it was said by some that John had been raised from the dead,

00:50.080 --> 00:54.960
by some that Elijah had appeared, and by others that one of the prophets of old had risen.

00:55.480 --> 00:56.240
Herod said,

00:57.020 --> 01:02.860
John, I beheaded, but who is this about whom I hear such things?

01:03.440 --> 01:05.260
And he sought to see him.

01:06.260 --> 01:09.860
On their return, the apostles told him all that they had done,

01:10.420 --> 01:13.760
and he took them and withdrew apart to a town called Bethsaida.

01:14.540 --> 01:16.780
When the crowds learned it, they followed him,

01:17.020 --> 01:19.980
and he welcomed them and spoke to them of the kingdom of God

01:19.980 --> 01:22.400
and cured those who had need of healing.

01:22.400 --> 01:25.080
Now the day began to wear away,

01:25.080 --> 01:27.060
and the twelve came and said to him,

01:27.920 --> 01:31.180
Send the crowd away to go into the surrounding villages and countryside

01:31.180 --> 01:36.220
to find lodging and get provisions, for we are here in a desolate place.

01:36.980 --> 01:38.000
But he said to them,

01:38.700 --> 01:40.720
You give them something to eat.

01:41.440 --> 01:42.140
They said,

01:42.900 --> 01:46.080
We have no more than five loaves and two fish,

01:46.680 --> 01:49.300
unless we are to go and buy food for all these people.

01:50.040 --> 01:52.460
For there were about five thousand men.

01:52.460 --> 01:54.520
And he said to his disciples,

01:55.080 --> 01:58.560
Have them sit down in groups, of about fifty each.

01:59.040 --> 02:02.140
And they did so, and had them all sit down.

02:02.680 --> 02:05.040
And taking the five loaves and the two fish,

02:05.260 --> 02:07.800
he looked up to heaven and said a blessing over them.

02:08.500 --> 02:12.240
Then he broke the loaves and gave them to the disciples to set before the crowd.

02:12.940 --> 02:15.100
And they all ate and were satisfied.

02:16.140 --> 02:20.580
And what was left over was picked up, twelve baskets of broken pieces.

02:21.840 --> 02:24.540
Now it happened that as he was praying alone,

02:25.080 --> 02:26.380
the disciples were with him.

02:26.900 --> 02:27.980
And he asked them,

02:28.700 --> 02:30.620
Who do the crowds say that I am?

02:31.100 --> 02:32.180
And they answered,

02:32.900 --> 02:35.820
John the Baptist, but others say Elijah.

02:36.420 --> 02:39.520
And others that one of the prophets of old has risen.

02:40.420 --> 02:41.360
Then he said to them,

02:42.120 --> 02:44.100
But who do you say that I am?

02:44.740 --> 02:45.900
And Peter answered,

02:46.700 --> 02:48.460
The Christ of God.

02:48.840 --> 02:53.880
And he strictly charged and commanded them to tell this to no one, saying,

02:53.880 --> 02:57.220
The Son of Man must suffer many things,

02:57.700 --> 03:01.340
and be rejected by the elders and chief priests and scribes,

03:01.780 --> 03:02.540
and be killed,

03:03.200 --> 03:05.820
and on the third day be raised.

03:06.480 --> 03:07.660
And he said to all,

03:08.380 --> 03:10.360
If anyone would come after me,

03:10.840 --> 03:14.620
let him deny himself and take up his cross daily and follow me.

03:15.160 --> 03:17.860
For whoever would save his life will lose it,

03:18.220 --> 03:21.540
but whoever loses his life for my sake will save it.

03:22.100 --> 03:23.860
For what does it profit a man,

03:24.400 --> 03:25.900
if he gains the whole world,

03:26.180 --> 03:28.400
and loses or forfeits himself?

03:29.620 --> 03:33.400
For whoever is ashamed of me and of my words,

03:33.400 --> 03:35.660
of him will the Son of Man be ashamed,

03:36.020 --> 03:37.500
when he comes in his glory,

03:37.800 --> 03:40.440
and the glory of the Father and of the holy angels.

03:41.140 --> 03:42.640
But I tell you truly,

03:42.800 --> 03:45.640
there are some standing here who will not taste death

03:45.640 --> 03:48.300
until they see the kingdom of God.

03:50.040 --> 03:52.540
Now about eight days after these sayings,

03:52.620 --> 03:53.520
he took with him Peter,

03:53.860 --> 03:54.960
and John and James,

03:55.180 --> 03:56.960
and went up on the mountain to pray.

03:57.480 --> 03:58.660
And as he was praying,

03:59.100 --> 04:01.080
the appearance of his face was altered,

04:01.580 --> 04:03.920
and his clothing became dazzling white.

04:05.020 --> 04:05.840
And behold,

04:06.300 --> 04:07.880
two men were talking with him,

04:08.360 --> 04:09.660
Moses and Elijah,

04:10.120 --> 04:12.800
who appeared in glory and spoke of his departure,

04:12.800 --> 04:15.480
which he was about to accomplish at Jerusalem.

04:16.220 --> 04:19.780
Now Peter and those who were with him were heavy with sleep,

04:20.280 --> 04:22.040
but when they became fully awake,

04:22.380 --> 04:23.640
they saw his glory,

04:23.860 --> 04:25.660
and the two men who stood with him.

04:26.220 --> 04:28.360
And as the men were parting from him,

04:28.660 --> 04:29.780
Peter said to Jesus,

04:30.620 --> 04:33.540
Master, it is good that we are here.

04:34.140 --> 04:35.460
Let us make three tents,

04:35.660 --> 04:36.580
one for you,

04:36.820 --> 04:37.760
and one for Moses,

04:38.060 --> 04:39.180
and one for Elijah.

04:40.100 --> 04:41.560
Not knowing what he said,

04:42.180 --> 04:43.840
as he was saying these things,

04:43.840 --> 04:46.340
a cloud came and overshadowed them,

04:46.820 --> 04:49.200
and they were afraid as they entered the cloud.

04:49.640 --> 04:52.040
And a voice came out of the cloud, saying,

04:52.540 --> 04:53.840
This is my son,

04:53.860 --> 04:55.840
my chosen one.

04:56.580 --> 04:57.720
Listen to him.

04:58.300 --> 04:59.860
And when the voice had spoken,

05:00.480 --> 05:01.900
Jesus was found alone.

05:02.460 --> 05:03.660
And they kept silent,

05:04.000 --> 05:07.340
and told no one in those days anything of what they had seen.

05:08.320 --> 05:09.640
On the next day,

05:10.040 --> 05:11.840
when they had come down from the mountain,

05:12.260 --> 05:13.800
a great crowd met him.

05:14.280 --> 05:15.020
And behold,

05:15.280 --> 05:17.080
a man from the crowd cried out,

05:17.680 --> 05:18.420
Teacher,

05:18.980 --> 05:21.080
I beg you to look at my son,

05:21.680 --> 05:23.300
for he is my only child.

05:23.860 --> 05:24.880
And behold,

05:25.020 --> 05:26.420
a spirit seizes him,

05:26.600 --> 05:28.320
and he suddenly cries out.

05:28.800 --> 05:30.020
It convulses him,

05:30.120 --> 05:31.460
so that he foams at the mouth,

05:31.800 --> 05:32.780
and shatters him,

05:33.120 --> 05:34.580
and will hardly leave him.

05:35.020 --> 05:37.840
And I begged your disciples to cast it out,

05:38.180 --> 05:39.400
but they could not.

05:40.380 --> 05:41.400
Jesus answered,

05:42.240 --> 05:45.280
O faithless and twisted generation,

05:45.840 --> 05:48.800
how long am I to be with you and bear with you?

05:49.340 --> 05:50.380
Bring your son here.

05:51.060 --> 05:52.020
While he was coming,

05:52.020 --> 05:53.840
the demon threw him to the ground,

05:53.860 --> 05:55.120
and convulsed him.

05:55.660 --> 05:57.760
But Jesus rebuked the unclean spirit,

05:58.120 --> 05:59.020
and healed the boy,

05:59.320 --> 06:00.800
and gave him back to his father.

06:01.460 --> 06:04.420
And all were astonished at the majesty of God.

06:05.100 --> 06:08.020
But while they were all marveling at everything he was doing,

06:08.600 --> 06:10.100
Jesus said to his disciples,

06:11.060 --> 06:14.120
Let these words sink into your ears.

06:14.940 --> 06:18.860
The Son of Man is about to be delivered into the hands of men.

06:19.540 --> 06:21.280
But they did not understand this saying,

06:21.520 --> 06:22.940
and it was concealed from them,

06:22.940 --> 06:23.840
so that they,

06:23.860 --> 06:25.020
they might not perceive it.

06:25.820 --> 06:28.200
And they were afraid to ask him about this saying.

06:29.260 --> 06:30.880
An argument arose among them,

06:31.120 --> 06:32.940
as to which of them was the greatest.

06:33.560 --> 06:34.240
But Jesus,

06:34.460 --> 06:36.060
knowing the reasoning of their hearts,

06:36.400 --> 06:38.540
took a child and put him by his side,

06:39.100 --> 06:40.080
and said to them,

06:40.880 --> 06:44.480
Whoever receives this child in my name receives me,

06:44.940 --> 06:47.520
and whoever receives me receives him who sent me.

06:47.960 --> 06:50.660
For he who is least among you all

06:50.660 --> 06:52.660
is the one who is great.

06:53.500 --> 06:53.800
John,

06:53.860 --> 06:54.860
the first of the disciples,

06:54.860 --> 06:54.940
answered,

06:54.940 --> 06:55.580
Master,

06:55.900 --> 06:58.640
we saw someone casting out demons in your name,

06:58.900 --> 07:00.300
and we tried to stop him

07:00.300 --> 07:02.260
because he does not follow with us.

07:02.840 --> 07:04.100
But Jesus said to him,

07:04.620 --> 07:06.120
Do not stop him,

07:06.600 --> 07:09.960
for the one who is not against you is for you.

07:11.540 --> 07:14.060
When the days drew near for him to be taken up,

07:14.440 --> 07:16.320
he set his face to go to Jerusalem.

07:17.120 --> 07:19.260
And he sent messengers ahead of him

07:19.260 --> 07:21.780
who went and entered a village of the Samaritans

07:21.780 --> 07:23.440
to make preparations for him.

07:23.860 --> 07:28.600
But the people did not receive him, because his face was set toward Jerusalem.

07:29.260 --> 07:32.540
And when his disciples James and John saw it, they said,

07:33.240 --> 07:37.160
Lord, do you want us to tell fire to come down from heaven and consume them?

07:37.460 --> 07:40.740
But he turned and rebuked them, and they went on to another village.

07:41.360 --> 07:44.580
As they were going along the road, someone said to him,

07:45.100 --> 07:47.300
I will follow you wherever you go.

07:47.840 --> 07:49.260
And Jesus said to him,

07:50.060 --> 07:53.460
Foxes have holes, and birds of the air have nests.

07:54.140 --> 07:56.840
But the Son of Man has nowhere to lay his head.

07:57.580 --> 07:58.760
To another he said,

07:59.480 --> 08:00.360
Follow me.

08:00.960 --> 08:01.760
But he said,

08:02.440 --> 08:04.960
Lord, let me first go and bury my father.

08:05.360 --> 08:07.100
And Jesus said to him,

08:07.960 --> 08:09.920
Leave the dead to bury their own dead.

08:10.280 --> 08:14.080
But as for you, go and proclaim the kingdom of God.

08:14.800 --> 08:15.940
Yet another said,

08:16.800 --> 08:21.580
I will follow you, Lord, but let me first say farewell to those at my home.

08:22.380 --> 08:23.420
Jesus said to him,

08:23.860 --> 08:28.800
No one who puts his hand to the plow and looks back is fit for the kingdom of God.

08:31.460 --> 08:32.460
The End

